From: PwndaWallet swap sidecar
Date: 2026-09-03
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] basicswap: BCH account-key glue (Grove-only, docs)

Grove-only embedder policy, deliberately NOT part of the BCH upstream-PR
candidate (PWNDA-PATCH-18): makes the C8 account-key path's behaviour for BCH
explicit and load-bearing for future maintainers.

Investigated rather than assumed, and the investigation is the deliverable:
both things this patch was expected to fix turned out to need NO functional
change. `_pwndaAddressType` is a plain coin_type-keyed dict lookup with no
allow-list to extend, and PWNDA-PATCH-18's `_deriveAddress` BCH branch is
checked -- and returns -- BEFORE PWNDA-PATCH-3's p2pkh branch is ever reached,
for ANY caller including `initializeFromAccountKey`. Proved with a standalone
script driving the real `initialize()` / `initializeFromAccountKey()` methods
from the same seed (byte-identical CashAddr output on both paths), plus a
negative control that reproduced the predicted failure when the branch was
disabled. This patch is therefore three comment-only insertions in
`wallet_manager.py` that make the branch-ordering invariant explicit, rather
than a manufactured functional change.

RECONSTRUCTED 2026-09-03: this file was lost from `upstream/patches/` by an
orchestrating-session mistake (moved aside during an abandoned experiment, then
deleted with the scratch directory that held it). The patch BODY below was
